{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your doctors here. You came in with chest pain and trouble breathing. Can I ask what brought you to the hospital tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve been feeling short of breath, especially when I lie down. I need three pillows to sleep. And this chest tightness—it’s been there a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Is the chest pain worse with movement or breathing deeply?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:18:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s not sharp. Just a constant pressure. Feels worse lying flat. And I’ve been coughing—dry, no mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:19:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any swelling in your legs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:19:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, a little. More than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:20:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your lungs and heart. Your chest X-ray shows fluid in the lungs—pulmonary edema. That’s likely why you’re short of breath. This is related to your heart not pumping well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:22:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My heart again? I thought I was doing okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a flare-up. We think it might be from eating more salty foods recently—like the cheeseburgers and chips you mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… yeah, I did have some of that. Didn’t think it’d do that much harm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Salt makes your body hold onto fluid, which makes your heart work harder. We’ve started you on a strong diuretic—Lasix—to help remove the extra fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:26:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your EKG and troponin levels. No sign of a heart attack. The pain is likely from the heart strain and fluid buildup. It should improve as we reduce the fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed your kidney function is a bit worse—creatinine is 2.6, up from your usual 1.7. That’s common when the heart isn’t pumping well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:32:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s something we’re watching. As your heart improves, your kidneys usually do too. We’ll keep checking your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my blood sugar? I’ve been checking it. It’s been high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:34:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. Glucose was 169 on admission. We know you’re on insulin. We’ll adjust your dose to keep it under control while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I try to stay on top of it, but it’s hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:37:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help. We’ve started you on 45 units of glargine insulin twice daily, plus sliding scale. We’ll make sure you’re comfortable managing it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:38:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ve also had some diarrhea—golden-colored, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:39:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noted that. No signs of infection—your blood cultures were negative. It’s likely not serious, but we’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my ankle—it’s been hurting. I think I might have twisted it a while back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-12-12 04:42:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll mention that to ortho. You may need a repeat X-ray after discharge if it’s still bothering you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I’m not as short of breath. I think the Lasix is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your breathing has improved. We’re switching you from IV Lasix to oral torsemide—80 mg twice a day. It’s stronger and lasts longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:18:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Same as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:19:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with that dose. We’ll also keep your digoxin and losartan. But we’re not adding a beta-blocker right now because of your past cocaine use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t used cocaine in a month, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:22:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. We’ll support you with that. Staying off it helps your heart and lungs a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m trying. Smoking’s harder, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:24:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can help with that too. There are programs and medications to support quitting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Maybe later. What about my blood work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:27:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is coming down—now 2.0. That’s a good sign your kidneys are recovering as your heart improves."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:28:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-12-13 08:29:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still a bit high, but better. We’ll keep the insulin dose we started. You’re checking it regularly—that’s excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You’re doing well. Your breathing is much better, and your leg swelling is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I feel lighter. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. We’ll switch your torsemide to 160 mg once daily. And we’re adding benzonatate for your cough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my cholesterol? I used to take a statin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. We’re adding pravastatin 40 mg daily. It helps protect your heart long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. And my insulin—will I keep the same dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 45 units twice daily, plus sliding scale. Your sugars have been in range the last two checks—that’s great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:08:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep doing that. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Weigh yourself every morning. If you gain more than 3 pounds in a day or two, call your doctor. Watch for shortness of breath, swelling, or chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And salt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-12-14 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stick to a low-salt diet. No chips, fast food, or processed meals. The nutrition team will go over this with you before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. You’ve done really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending you home with your meds, including the new insulin dose, torsemide, pravastatin, and benzonatate. Keep checking your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll weigh myself every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:04:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And follow up with your primary doctor soon. If you can stay off cocaine and reduce smoking, your heart will keep improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:06:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-12-15 10:07:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-12-12 03:56:00",
